<title>EGYPT: Egyptian pound interbank rates rise.</title>
<headline>Egyptian pound interbank rates rise.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound rose on Sunday to between 10-3/16 and 10-5/16 percent from Thursday's range of 9-3/4 and 10 percent in a traditionally short private-sector market at the start of the week, bankers said.</p>
<p>One-week rates also went up to a range of 10-5/16 and 10-7/16 percent from 10 and 10-1/4 percent on Thursday, the bankers added.</p>
<p>State-owned banks kept their minimum interbank lending rate at 10-1/2 percent, they said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
